  "details": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxen-netback: defer xenvif_mcast_addr_list_free()\n\nIn order for the function to legitimately avoid locking/RCU, it needs to\nrun after all TX/RX processing has finished/stopped: Lookups happen from\nxenvif_start_xmit(), while adds/removes happen from xenvif_tx_action()\n(called out of xenvif_poll()).\n\nMove the call out of xenvif_disconnect_data() (the call to the function\nfrom connect()'s error path doesn't require any cleaning up there), and\nput it past the synchronization point in backend_disconnect().\n\nThis is XSA-527 / CVE-2026-100081.",
